{
    "note": [
        "One repair, one row, read by both engines that still repair a torn tool call.",
        "`repairedBy` names which one owns it, and both suites assert both halves of that:",
        "`worker` means scripts/tool-call-repair.mjs turns `wrote` into `becomes`; `schema` means",
        "the generated grammar refuses `wrote` outright, so nothing rewrites it and the model has to",
        "write `becomes` itself.",
        "The split is not a preference and is no longer a prose comment either. The agent loop",
        "validates a call against the generated schema between `prepareArguments` and the router,",
        "so a shape the schema refuses never reaches Rust and only the worker can answer it.",
        "`the line between the two engines is the schema's` in tool-call-repair.test.mjs computes",
        "that for every row here with pi-ai's own `validateToolArguments` — the function the loop",
        "calls — and refuses a row the worker repairs that the schema would have let through.",
        "There was a third engine: a repairing table in Rust behind the schema. It changed 0 of 3,199",
        "recorded entries once every entry and every tagged payload was closed, and it is deleted.",
        "The two rows it owned are the schema's now."
    ],
    "repairs": [
        {
            "why": "a key that swallowed its own value, separated by a space",
            "tool": "godot_logs",
            "op": "read",
            "wrote": {
                "limit 50": null
            },
            "becomes": {
                "limit": 50
            },
            "repairedBy": "schema"
        },
        {
            "why": "a key that swallowed its own value, concatenated and said twice",
            "tool": "godot_logs",
            "op": "read",
            "wrote": {
                "minSeverityWarning": "warning"
            },
            "becomes": {
                "minSeverity": "warning"
            },
            "repairedBy": "schema"
        },
        {
            "why": "a key that swallowed a whole JSON value",
            "tool": "godot_resource",
            "op": "create_shape",
            "wrote": {
                "path": "res://a.tres",
                "shapeType": "RectangleShape2D",
                "size [16, 16]": null
            },
            "becomes": {
                "path": "res://a.tres",
                "shapeType": "RectangleShape2D",
                "size": [16, 16]
            },
            "repairedBy": "schema"
        },
        {
            "why": "the same pair torn twice, the second one saying nothing new",
            "tool": "godot_resource",
            "op": "create_shape",
            "wrote": {
                "path": "res://a.tres",
                "shapeType RectangleShape2D": null,
                "size [640, 16]": null
